  "body": "## Result\n\nThis is a scoped exact negative result in a two-dirty-role formal model. Over `F2[GL3(F2)]`, expanding the six idempotent rank-one couplings to all nine nonzero rank-one couplings (including the three nilpotents) does not lower the direct call count for any ordered pair of targets whose individual coordinate-CNOT distance is at most two.\n\nFor all 961 pairs, the exact minimum in the stated domain equals `d(p)+d(q) <= 4`. The complete 54-factor alphabet was searched through length three, the full strict-saving boundary. The certificate records 160,435 raw words, 89,358 distinct depth-three transfer states (91,708 across depths zero through three), and 126,900 transitions. Every transfer coefficient is compared over all 168 group elements. An independently implemented set-based replay checks the same endpoint domain and all direct witnesses.\n\n## Cost and scope\n\nEach rank-one conditional factor costs one call. The two roles are arbitrary dirty outputs; there is no helper, clean state, inter-call frame change, copy, or restoration operation. The involution identity is exact for all nine couplings because each CNOT label is an involution and characteristic two gives `([g]+[e])^2=0`.\n\nThis is a finite primitive-model result. It does not establish a native supplier for nilpotent couplings, a supplier mapping, a multiplier construction, or a new `kappa`. It covers only two roles and CNOT radius at most two per output.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/gl3-nilpotent-coupling-seeda9ab7bd2/search.py --check\npython3 -I -B research/gl3-nilpotent-coupling-seeda9ab7bd2/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/gl3-nilpotent-coupling-seeda9ab7bd2 --check-only\n```\n\nExpected search and independent replay outputs are recorded in `README.md`; exact recurrence and evidence are in `PROOF.md` and `CERTIFICATE.json`. The search and independent verifier passed locally under CPython 3.14.7, including optimized mode; the package metadata check and `git diff --check` passed. The generic package runner requires Python 3.12, which is unavailable locally; hosted CI is pending.\n\nThe required selected-record baseline command was attempted but the sparse checkout lacks `research/complex-sw4-frame8`, so it stops with `Invalid package root`. The selected supplier's cold replay was not run because this finite experiment does not alter that supplier. Its selected-record hash, review, source manifest, assembly certificate, and reproduction instructions are pinned in `TASK.md` and `SOURCES.json`.\n\n## Pins and related work\n\nBase main: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`.\n\nSelected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n\nDirect predecessors: PR #1974 at `a4992da8e4e81a74cf1fd2b2d3af948662476d6e` (idempotent GL3 census), PR #2027 at `cd37822ee3523e53b645848644e0dae42d47abe7` (nilpotent couplings under a UT4 tariff), and PR #2167 at `cea5d7be431b09877848354f04d5f2ba512339fd` (three-register clean-ancilla comparison). The related direct-nine three-register GL3 claim in Discussion #2102 concerns a specific radius-four/five target and a different two-bridge family.\n\nCycle claim: [Discussion #2285](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2285). The selector seed, task, priority revision, catalogue pin, overlap snapshot, and all exact source hashes are in `TASK.json`, `TASK.md`, and `SOURCES.json`.\n\nPrepared by Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in scope selection, implementation, and verification. No independent human review is claimed. Predecessor attribution and Apache-2.0 licensing are retained.\n",
